&lt;p&gt;Chaque jour, dans plus de 2 000 magasins et plus de 70 pays, des millions de prix changent. Une erreur, c’est un client mal servi, un magasin en difficulté et de la confiance perdue. Notre rôle : identifier et transmettre le bon prix, au bon moment, sans erreur, partout dans le monde.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nos 2 produits critiques tournent 24/7, avec un SLA supérieur à 99,9 %. Autour d’eux, 4 autres produits exploitent les données de vente et proposent des leviers de dynamisme commercial aux magasins.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tu rejoindras une plateforme event-driven qui évolue en continu pour répondre à des enjeux de performance, de résilience et de qualité. Au sein de l’équipe, tu contribueras concrètement à cette ambition en développant et en faisant évoluer nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tu conçois, développes et maintiens des fonctionnalités backend en Java ou Kotlin, en lien avec les besoins produit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tu participes à la conception de solutions robustes pour nos systèmes distribués et nos flux Kafka.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tu contribues à la qualité du code par les tests, les revues de code et le partage de bonnes pratiques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tu prends part aux décisions techniques de l’équipe et documentes les choix importants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tu participes à l’amélioration continue de la performance, de l’observabilité et de la résilience de nos services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tu contribues à l’exploitation de nos produits en production : investigation, suivi des alertes et résolution des incidents, avec le soutien de l’équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tu travailles en étroite collaboration avec les Software Engineers, le Product Manager, l’Engineering Manager, le QE et le Support Engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;STACK TECHNIQUE&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Java, Kotlin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kafka, architecture event-driven, microservices, APIs REST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PostgreSQL, Valkey (cache)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Docker, Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub Actions (CI), Flux (GitOps / CD)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Datadog (monitoring et alerting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus : React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience significative en développement backend, avec une solide pratique de Java ou Kotlin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une première expérience avec Kafka, ou une forte envie de progresser sur le streaming et les systèmes distribués.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Le souci de produire un code lisible, testé et maintenable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une sensibilité aux enjeux de performance, de disponibilité et de fiabilité en production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une première familiarité avec Docker, Kubernetes, la CI/CD ou l’observabilité.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;L’envie d’apprendre, de partager tes idées et de contribuer aux décisions techniques de l’équipe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un anglais professionnel (B2) pour collaborer avec des équipes dans le monde entier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;CE QUE NOUS T’OFFRONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un impact concret et visible : ton travail compte dans les magasins Decathlon du monde entier.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une culture de la performance et de l’autonomie inspirée d’Accelerate : Kanban, livraison continue et amélioration continue de nos produits. Plus de 20 livraisons en production par semaine, avec un cycle time moyen de moins de 4 jours sur l’année.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GitHub Copilot avec les derniers modèles d’IA, et Gemini, dans ton quotidien de dev.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un mode de travail hybride et flexible, avec des bureaux à Nantes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du matériel au choix (Mac, Windows ou Chromebook).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Des certifications techniques dès la première année, des conférences externes (DevFest…) et de grandes conférences tech internes, du temps dédié à la veille et une mobilité internationale possible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une rémunération attractive, avec des bonus mensuels et trimestriels et l’actionnariat salarié.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tu ne coches pas toutes les cases ? Postule quand même, on en discute.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imaginez si la technologie nous permettait de repousser les frontières et d&#39;offrir des expériences sportives inédites. C&#39;est précisément notre ambition chez Decathlon Digital ! Nous sommes une équipe de plus de 5 000 experts en ingénierie logicielle, gestion de produits, données, cloud et cybersécurité, répartis à Paris, Lille et Amsterdam. Ensemble, nous créons la plus vaste plateforme sportive numérique, en exploitant les innovations technologiques pour optimiser la chaîne de valeur, concevoir des expériences connectées et donner une seconde vie à nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering  Nantes, Loire-Atlantique

Associate Director, Clinical Supply Management (UK/EU) &lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Summit:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summit Therapeutics Inc. is a biopharmaceutical oncology company with a mission focused on improving quality of life, increasing potential duration of life, and resolving serious unmet medical needs. At Summit, we believe in building a team of world class professionals who are passionate about this mission, and it is our people who drive this mission to reality. Summit’s core values include integrity, passion for excellence, purposeful urgency, collaboration, and our commitment to people. Our employees are truly the heart and soul of our culture, and they are invaluable in shaping our journey toward excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summit’s team is inspired to touch and help change lives through Summit’s clinical studies in the field of oncology. Summit has multiple global Phase 3 clinical studies, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-small Cell Lung Cancer (NSCLC)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi: Phase 3 clinical study which was intended to evaluate ivonescimab combined with chemotherapy compared to placebo plus chemotherapy in patients with EGFR-mutated, locally advanced or metastatic non-squamous NSCLC who were previously treated with a 3rd generation EGFR TKI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi-3: Phase 3 clinical study which is intended to evaluate ivonescimab combined with chemotherapy compared to pembrolizumab combined with chemotherapy in patients with first-line metastatic NSCLC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi-7: Phase 3 clinical study which is intended to evaluate ivonescimab monotherapy compared to pembrolizumab monotherapy in patients with first-line metastatic NSCLC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Colorectal Cancer (CRC)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HARMONi-GI3: Phase 3 clinical study intended to evaluate ivonescimab in combination with chemotherapy compared with bevacizumab plus chemotherapy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ivonescimab is an investigational therapy not presently approved by any regulatory authority other than China’s National Medical Products Administration (NMPA). Summit is headquartered in Miami, Florida, and has additional offices in California, New Jersey, the UK, and Ireland.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt;&quot;&gt;Job Title: Sr. Medical Science Liaison&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10.5pt;&quot;&gt;Location: Oxford, UK or Zug, Switzerland or Dublin, Ireland&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview of Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director, Clinical Supply Management supports the Senior Director in leading the full scope of global clinical supply chain responsibilities. The role translates functional strategy into disciplined execution across demand and supply planning, inventory management, packaging and labelling, distribution, returns and destruction, cross-border compliance, and GxP operations. Acting as a key delegate for the Senior Director, the (Associate) Director provides a layer of management for direct reports, establishes clear priorities and performance expectations, develops team capability, and drives operational excellence through standardized processes, meaningful metrics, proactive risk management, and continuous improvement. The role partners closely with Clinical Operations, Commercial, CMC, Quality, Regulatory, Finance, Legal, Procurement, Medical Affairs and Program Management, and oversees external partners including Contract Development and Manufacturing Organizations (CDMOs), IXRS providers and specialist service providers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the Senior Director in developing functional strategy, operating plans, budgets, governance and performance objectives across global clinical supply chain activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads day-to-day execution for new and ongoing studies and products, ensuring robust forecasting, supply planning, schedule adherence, inventory optimization, global logistics and sustained GxP compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as a delegate for the Senior Director in cross-functional forums, governance meetings, supplier reviews and issue escalation, providing clear recommendations and ensuring timely follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages and develops direct reports, translating functional priorities into individual objectives, balancing workloads, coaching performance, supporting career development and ensuring appropriate succession and capability plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creates an effective management layer by coordinating team activities, reinforcing accountability, removing operational barriers and escalating material risks or decisions to the Senior Director.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overseeing the Clinical Supply Management (CSM) team, the Associate Director interprets complex clinical protocols, development plans and commercial demand forecasts, working with CMC and internal and external partners to develop packaging, labelling, supply and resupply strategies, timelines and plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the accountability of CSM team to oversee packaging, labelling, release, distribution, resupply, returns, reconciliation and destruction activities across global locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develops and maintains supply project budgets, resource plans and integrated schedules, monitors performance and proactively resolves variances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages CDMO and service-provider activities from RFP and contracting support through routine operations, troubleshooting, invoicing and performance management using defined KPIs and service expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports IXRS selection, design, set-up, User Acceptance Testing (UAT), implementation and ongoing operational performance as required by IRT Management Team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives operational excellence by defining standard work, governance routines, KPIs and dashboards; uses trend and root-cause analysis to improve service, quality, cost, compliance and team productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads continuous-improvement initiatives that streamline and harmonize processes, strengthen inspection readiness and embed sustainable ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports regulatory submissions, audits and inspections and ensures timely management of SOPs, change controls, deviations, investigations and CAPAs within the function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provides continuity of leadership and performs other responsibilities within the function as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience, Education and Specialized Knowledge and Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc, MSc, engineering or pharmacy degree, or equivalent, with a minimum of 8+ years of progressive supply chain experience in a pharmaceutical, biotechnology or contract development and manufacturing organization (CDMO) environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading complex international clinical studies and product supply chains, with broad knowledge of regulatory and GMP requirements for IMP and commercial product packaging and supply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior people-management experience, including setting objectives, coaching performance, developing talent, delegating effectively and managing through others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate strategy into executable priorities, operating rhythms, metrics and measurable team outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational-excellence and continuous-improvement capability, including process standardization, KPI management, root-cause analysis and sustainable implementation of improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of IXRS design specifications, set-up and UAT, together with proficiency in clinical supply planning and forecasting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project, budget, risk and resource-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining high-quality results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in outsourcing, supplier governance, negotiation and performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, scaling or improving end-to-end product supply chains and associated business processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate as a trusted deputy to the Director, exercise sound judgement within delegated authority and escalate issues with clear options and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator able to influence all levels of the organization and build effective relationships with global colleagues, customers and suppliers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work independently with complex global problems while fostering inclusion, collaboration, accountability and effective team leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile and resilient in a dynamic organization where priorities may change rapidly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the drug development process and applicable FDA, EMA and PMDA expectations, including GMP, GCP, Annex 13 and relevant clinical trial requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically proficient with industry-standard systems and tools and able to use technology, data and industry trends to improve efficiency and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledgeable of and compliant with SOPs, change controls, deviations, investigations and CAPAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is the pay for this position&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Transparency&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$83,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$97,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actual compensation packages are based on several factors that are unique to each candidate, including but not limited to skill set, depth of experience, certifications, and specific work location. This may be different in other locations due to differences in the cost of labor. The total compensation package for this position may also include bonus, stock, benefits and/or other applicable variable compensation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Summit does not accept referrals from employment businesses and/or employment agencies in respect of the vacancies posted on this site. All employment businesses/agencies are required to contact Summit’s Talent Acquisition team at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----- ----- obtain prior written authorization before referring any candidates to Summit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Summit Therapeutics Inc.&amp;nbsp;is an Equal Opportunity Employer and takes pride in creating and maintaining diverse environment. We do not discriminate in recruitment, hiring, training or promotion or any other employment practices for reasons of race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, sexual orientation, marital or veteran status, disability, or any other legally protected status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Supply Chain  Oxford, UK, Dublin Ireland

Fullstack Web Developer &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Fullstack Web Developer to join our Web Apps team, in our Zürich office. In this role you will have the opportunity to drive development of new features, have a say in architecture and design decisions and have real impact across all the team’s projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The web apps team plays a central role at Auterion and owns the systems that add connectivity and remote interfaces for fleet management and operations. Our services are responsible for ingesting and analyzing flight telemetry data, managing and updating the fleet as well as integrating with other systems across the stack.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who’s a self-starter, can work independently, can work with ambiguity, can take decisions on their own and not be afraid to drive and push towards getting the project across the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership and drive the development of new features across all the team’s web based projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean, readable and maintainable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate services between edge devices and our centralized services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle new feature discovery, prototyping and investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Customer Success team in debugging and resolving customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze user usage patterns and other statistics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push initiatives to clean up, upgrade, and refactor existing services to reduce technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve integrations with 3rd party services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in a Fullstack web development or similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with the Node.js&amp;nbsp; ecosystem, development and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with the Typescript ecosystem, development and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with modern SPAs (Vue.js ecosystem preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Postgres/SQL (queries, transactions, views, indexes, triggers) as well as ORM systems (Prisma)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Docker and container orchestration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with CI/CD pipelines (GoCD and GH Actions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monitoring and observability tools (Datadog, Grafana)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Python proficiency is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CH/EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a> Engineering  Zurich

Senior Software Engineer (Agentic Search) - Web Access Engineer &lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;About &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;heading 2&quot;&gt;Tavily&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134245418&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245529&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:160,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:80}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We&#39;re&amp;nbsp;building the infrastructure layer for agentic web interaction at scale. Our API is designed from the ground up to power Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and real-time reasoning in AI systems. By connecting LLMs to high-quality, trustworthy web content, we help developers build agents that are not only intelligent — but also informed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We work with some of the most innovative teams in AI — from small startups shaping the ecosystem to the largest enterprises deploying AI at scale. Whether&amp;nbsp;it&#39;s&amp;nbsp;powering sales assistants, research copilots, or internal knowledge tools,&amp;nbsp;we&#39;re&amp;nbsp;the missing link between LLMs and the real world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to build the web access infrastructure behind a novel search engine designed for agentic AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;In this role, you will investigate how modern websites communicate with browsers and translate that understanding into production systems operating at internet scale. You will build browser infrastructure and tooling that enables reliable, efficient access to web content across a rapidly changing web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Research and analyse how modern websites communicate with browsers across the complete request lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Investigate browser fingerprinting, client verification mechanisms, and modern web technologies to enable reliable web access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Build tooling for browser instrumentation, debugging, observability, and large-scale experimentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Translate technical research into production systems operating at internet scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;You have 5+ years of experience as a software engineer working on production backend or infrastructure systems, and are an expert in several of the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Browser Technologies&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Chromium architecture and browser internals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Browser lifecycle and navigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium, or similar browser automation frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
